.TH BC 1
.SH NAME
bc \- arbitrary-precision arithmetic language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "bc [ \-c ] [ \-l ] [ file ... ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bc
is an interactive processor for a language which resembles C but provides unlimited precision arithmetic.
(For a tutorial, see ``Arbitrary Precision Desk Calculator Language (BC)'' in the
.I "Support Tools Guide.)
It takes input from any files given, then reads the standard input.
The
.B \-l
argument stands for the name of an arbitrary precision math library.
The syntax for
.B bc
programs is as follows; L means letter a\-z, E means expression, S means statement.
.PP
.TP 12
Comments
enclosed in /* and */
.TP
Names
simple variables: L
.br
array elements: L [ E ]
.br
The words
.BR ibase ,
.BR obase ,
and
.BR scale
.TP
Other operands
arbitrarily long numbers with optional sign and decimal point.
.br
( E )
.br
.B sqrt(
E
.B )
.br
